@node beamformer Plugin Developer Guide
@section Developer Guide

Beamformer plugin — MVDR, superdirective, and GSC beamformers.

@subsubheading What It Does

Combines signals from multiple microphones to focus on sound from a specific direction while rejecting noise and interference from other directions. Supports three beamforming algorithms for different use cases.

@subsubheading Features

@itemize @bullet
@item @strong{MVDR beamformer}: Minimum Variance Distortionless Response — optimal noise rejection
@item @strong{Superdirective beamformer}: Maximum directivity for diffuse noise fields
@item @strong{GSC beamformer}: Generalized Sidelobe Canceller — adaptive interference rejection
@item @strong{Configurable steering}: Point the beam in any direction
@end itemize


@subsubheading Architecture

@example
src/
├── lib.rs              # BeamformerPlugin
├── mvdr.rs             # MVDR beamformer
├── superdirective.rs   # Superdirective beamformer
├── gsc.rs              # Generalized Sidelobe Canceller
├── steering.rs         # Steering vector computation
└── params.rs           # Parameters
@end example


@subsubheading Testing

